-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/b96dc83c-b1cd-47ea-88a3-cdd3a48d85eb
-- title:
--   Expand a valid prefix into exactly its positive children
-- statement:
--   Let $w$ be a key-consistent wanted item for the raw incidences of finite sets $A,B,C$ with integer values. Fix a valid prefix $u$ at depth $k<J$, and let $\mathcal P(u)$ be its children whose next-prefix incidence count is positive, in the machine's enumeration order. Set $\rho=2h(J-k-1)$ and $G=\binom{2h}{h}$.
--
--   Assume exact source zeta stages and the level-$(k+1)$ sorted catalog, pointer row, and box stages. Its threshold $t$ and cutoff $b$ satisfy $t\le\rho+1$, $b\le\rho$, and $\rho-t\le b$. The prescribed separated buffers, query scratch, lookup and value word bounds hold, with $S\le W$ and depth allowance $2(512hJ)+16$. Then
--   $$r=|\mathcal P(u)|,\qquad\nu(\mathrm{out}_\ell+i)=\operatorname{mask}(P_\ell(\mathcal P(u)_i)),\quad\nu(\mathrm{out}_r+i)=\operatorname{mask}(P_r(\mathcal P(u)_i)).$$
--   Time is the catalog-expansion budget plus the pair-gather budget for $G$ entries and $120$. Below candidate scratch, memory outside the two populated output segments is unchanged.
--
--   This materializes exactly the surviving children for a reporting step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingPositiveExpand.lean#L42-L135

